// Old School's consumption timers, beside 377's own %eat_delay (food). Three timers, each the
// map_clock at or before which that kind of thing is refused - so the same test and the same
// "+2 means a 3-tick timer" arithmetic as %eat_delay (player/scripts/consumption/consume.rs2):
//
//   %eat_delay         food. 3 ticks. https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Food
//   %potion_delay      every potion. 3 ticks, and a timer of its own, so a potion goes down in
//                      the same tick as food but never in the same tick as another potion.
//                      https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Potions
//   %combo_food_delay  karambwans and gnome food. 3 ticks. They skip the food timer - that is
//                      what lets them follow a shark in the same tick - but set it, so nothing
//                      eats after them. https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Cooked_karambwan
//
// Temp: a timer is a few ticks long and means nothing after a logout.
[potion_delay]

[combo_food_delay]
